post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Little Big Mouse routes the mouse itself (it grabs the physical mice through
evdev and re-injects a corrected stream through a uinput virtual pointer), which
needs access to the input devices. Add yourself to the "input" group and log out
and back in:

    sudo gpasswd -a "$USER" input

Be aware that membership of the "input" group lets every program you run read
all keyboard and mouse events.

Without it the daemon falls back to the XDG InputCapture portal (Wayland) or
X11, which cannot intercept the cursor crossing between adjacent outputs on
KWin — the pointer will still jump natively at shared borders.

EOF
}
